{
  "extends": "../../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "lib": [
      "DOM",
      "DOM.Iterable",
      "ES2022"
    ],
    "jsx": "preserve",
    "noEmit": true,
    "incremental": true,
    "module": "ESNext",
    "plugins": [
      {
        "name": "next"
      }
    ],
    // Pin React's types to one copy, whatever npm does with hoisting.
    //
    // This monorepo holds two Reacts: apps/web is on 19, apps/mobile is on 18
    // because that is what Expo SDK 52 and React Native 0.76 support. npm
    // hoists one @types/react to the root and nests the other, and which one
    // lands where depends on the whole tree — so it can differ between a
    // developer's machine and a clean CI install of the same lockfile.
    //
    // When the two copies end up on opposite sides of a boundary, TypeScript
    // sees two unrelated ReactNode types and rejects perfectly ordinary code
    // with "'StatTile' cannot be used as a JSX component". That is what broke
    // the Vercel build while the identical commit compiled locally: the
    // deployment resolved next (and with it, React's types) from the root copy
    // that @sentry/nextjs's peer dependency added, and the app's own source
    // from the nested one.
    //
    // paths is program-wide, so every `import ... from "react"` in the build —
    // ours, Next's, Radix's — resolves to the same declarations. The array is
    // ordered: prefer this app's own copy, fall back to the root when npm
    // chose to hoist it instead. Either way there is exactly one identity.
    "paths": {
      "@/*": [
        "./src/*"
      ],
      "react": [
        "./node_modules/@types/react",
        "../../node_modules/@types/react"
      ],
      "react/*": [
        "./node_modules/@types/react/*",
        "../../node_modules/@types/react/*"
      ],
      "react-dom": [
        "./node_modules/@types/react-dom",
        "../../node_modules/@types/react-dom"
      ],
      "react-dom/*": [
        "./node_modules/@types/react-dom/*",
        "../../node_modules/@types/react-dom/*"
      ]
    },
    "allowJs": true
  },
  "include": [
    "next-env.d.ts",
    "**/*.ts",
    "**/*.tsx",
    ".next/types/**/*.ts"
  ],
  "exclude": [
    "node_modules"
  ]
}
